# This repository IS a threat-taxonomy corpus: every technique, attack class and
# evidence note DESCRIBES an attack, so HMA's regex secret/pattern detectors fire
# on the descriptive text itself. matrix.json:20, for example, is the
# credential-harvest tactic description ("Extract API keys, tokens, and
# credentials from agent context and connected services") — a definition of the
# attack, not a hardcoded secret. The data is public, machine-curated taxonomy
# and contains no credentials by construction.
#
# Same rationale as opena2a-registry/.hmaignore ("HMA's regex-based detector
# fires on security docs that describe attack patterns"). Scope is the taxonomy
# content only; scripts/ stays in scope so a real secret in maintenance code is
# still caught.
matrix.json
README.md
CHANGELOG.md
CONTRIBUTING.md
EVIDENCE_AUDIT.md
